From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm: don't adjust the white point for neutral night light

Neutral channel factors left a clamp in the color pipeline that
forced a gamma LUT onto every output.
---
--- a/src/backends/drm/drm_output.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/drm/drm_output.cpp
@@ -409,6 +409,9 @@ static QVector3D adaptChannelFactors(const std::shared_ptr<ColorDescription> &or
 
 static std::shared_ptr<ColorDescription> applyNightLight(const std::shared_ptr<ColorDescription> &originalColor, const QVector3D &sRGBchannelFactors)
 {
+    if (sRGBchannelFactors == QVector3D(1, 1, 1)) {
+        return originalColor;
+    }
     const QVector3D adapted = adaptChannelFactors(originalColor, sRGBchannelFactors);
     // calculate the white point
     // this includes the maximum brightness we can do without clipping any color channel as well
